# The database. Contains real accounts and password hashes — this must
# never reach a repo, and never sit anywhere a web server can serve it.
#
# THE PREFIX PATTERNS ARE THE IMPORTANT ONES. `*.db` only matches a name
# ENDING in .db, so a backup called elusion.db.before-something sailed
# straight past it and into a commit. A database copy is usually named by
# adding a suffix, which is exactly the shape *.db cannot see.
elusion.db
elusion.db.*
elusion*.db
*.db
*.db.*
*.db-journal

# SQLite's WAL sidecars. *.db-journal above covers rollback-journal mode, which
# is what this server uses today — but journal_mode=WAL produces elusion.db-wal
# and elusion.db-shm instead, and neither ends in .db or .db-journal. The -wal
# file holds transactions not yet folded into the database, which on a login or
# a registration means password hashes. One PRAGMA away from being live, so it
# is covered now rather than after.
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite*.*
*.bak

# Virtual environment — recreate with:
#   python -m venv venv && venv\Scripts\pip install -r requirements.txt
venv/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local overrides
.env
